  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...An upper ridge centered over the Southeast CONUS\nand sfc high pressure ridging in from the north will keep dry\nconditions across ENC through much of the work week. However,  \nupper low retrograding to the SSW across the offshore waters \nThursday into Friday may bring a few showers near the Gulf\nStream, but dry conditions expected to persist across land \nareas. NE winds will continue through mid week bringing \nseasonable temperatures and comfortable humidity levels through,\nthen will see gradually warming and increasing dewpoints \nThursday into Friday as high pressure weakens and slides \noffshore allowing low level flow to veer to southerly ahead of \nan approaching cold front. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A weak cold front will drop south into the area\nSaturday and briefly stall before lifting back north as a cold\nfront on Sunday. Sfc convergence and lowering heights aloft as \nshortwave energy rides over the upper ridge along with\nincreasing moisture will allow for a better chance of showers \nand thuderstorms across the area over the weekend and into early\nnext week, especially through peak heating when instability is \ngreatest.",
